1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,398
So: half of the apple is rotten, but half of the apples are rotten; most of the water has dried up, but most of the students have paid.

2
00:00:08,398 --> 00:00:10,781
And one pair to memorise.

3
00:00:10,781 --> 00:00:16,510
A number of means many, so it takes a plural verb: a number of tourists are waiting.

4
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:23,177
The number of is a single figure, so it takes a singular verb: the number of tourists is rising.

